+## What this does
+
+The model's index tool (`link-model-part`) can now take in old parts of the product model once a person approved it. Three steps had no tool, and the #1021 review of Orchestration (BI-9) was blocked on all three: its first capability takes in View plans, Manage a plan and Shape a slice.
+
+- **`thin: false`** takes a capability's or feature's thin mark off both places it lives, the index entry and the page's Thin line, so the part can take a full ICE of its own in the same request.
+- **`capability: <id>`** files a feature under another capability, one in the index or added earlier in the same request. Only a feature takes it.
+- **`doc: <new path>`** moves a page, and the ice.md beside it, to a new folder that a part of its kind may use; the entry's doc and its ICE entry's doc follow, and the old folder is removed. It is refused while any page or record names an old path (from the model root, or as a link relative to the page), while the old folder holds any other file, or when the new folder already holds a file. A failed write puts every file and folder back.
+- The skill's rule "Never re-parent" now reads that a feature with a capability moves only through this update, when a person approved taking in an old part; `link-model-gaps` leaves that move as alignment work. The `product-os-keeper` agent lists the three updates.
+
+The acceptance check (`.garura/project/issues/1037/evidence/eval/eval_1037.py`) was committed first, failing (5 of 26), and now passes 30 of 30. The skill's unit tests: 44, all passing. The component check reads 36 errors and 1 warning before and after, none in the files changed.
+
+Out of scope: writing BI-9's pages (#1021), the merge tool (`remove-model-part`), and a test of a move that fails part way (the reviewer forced two such failures in a scratch copy, and every file came back).
+
+## Raised past a failed self-review check
+
+The pre-push check (`check_self_review.py`) exited 1 on one line: commit 339ddf54 has a 156-character subject, and the commit rules cap it at 72. The product owner chose to raise it anyway, recorded in `.garura/project/issues/1037/context/raise-past-check.md`. The long subject stays in the history, and this run of /propose-change does not close COMPLETED.
+
+Closes #1037
+
